    "body": "> https://gist.github.com/foolip/eef626588ed75727c663e46902ff9fcb is the output of the mobile query. I think that if removing this is desirable, then the best next step would be for someone to try analyzing a random sample of these sites to see if they would break if behavior changed.\r\n\r\nHere's one site that is broken in Gecko due to this:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.satine.org/research/webkit/snowleopard/snowstack.html\r\n\r\nReported as [Gecko bug 1756417](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1756417)",
